" ``MIN_L``\\ =[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+] ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` ``MAX_L``\\ "
"=[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+] ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` "
"``ANGULAR_SCHEME=lebedev|legendre|lobatto\\\\`` ``ANGLEVEL``\\ =\\ *1*-*8* "
"``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` ``THRESHOLD_ANGULAR|GRIDTHR_ANG|ACCA=acca``"

msgid ""
"Specify the details of the angular quadrature scheme. The default choice for"
" *method* is ``LEBEDEV`` (ie. as in A. D. Becke, `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.454033>`__ **88**, 2547 (1988)) which provides"
" angular grids of octahedral symmetry. An alternative choice for *method* is"
" ``LEGENDRE``  ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` which gives Gauss-Legendre "
"quadrature in :math:`\\theta` and simple quadrature in :math:`\\phi`, as "
"defined by C. W. Murray, N. C. Handy and G. J. Laming, `Mol. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1080/00268979300100651>`__ **78**, 997 (1993). "
"Similarly, *method*\\ =\\ ``LOBATTO``\\ ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` defines a "
"spherical quadrature over :math:`\\theta` and :math:`\\phi` space using "
"Lobatto's formula and using the size reduction described by Treutler and "
"Ahlrichs `J. Chem. Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.469408>`__ **102**, "
"346 (1995). Both, *method*\\ =\\ ``LEGENDRE`` and ``LOBATTO`` are suitable "
"options if highly accurate angular integrations need to be performed."
msgstr ""
"指定角向求积格式的细节。\\ *method* 的默认选择是 ``LEBEDEV``\\ （即 A. D. Becke 所述，\\ `J. Chem. "
"Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.454033>`__ **88**, 2547 "
"(1988)），它提供具有八面体对称性的角向网格。\\ *method* 的另一种选择是 ``LEGENDRE``  "
"``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``\\ ，它在 :math:`\\theta` 方向给出 Gauss-Legendre 求积、在 "
":math:`\\phi` 方向给出简单求积，由 C. W. Murray, N. C. Handy and G. J. Laming 定义，\\ "
"`Mol. Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1080/00268979300100651>`__ **78**, 997 "
"(1993)。类似地，\\ *method*\\=\\ ``LOBATTO``\\ ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` 使用 "
"Lobatto 公式以及 Treutler 和 Ahlrichs `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.469408>`__ **102**, 346 (1995) 所述的尺寸缩减，在 "
":math:`\\theta` 和 :math:`\\phi` 空间上定义球面求积。如果需要进行高精度的角向积分，\\ *method*\\=\\ "
"``LEGENDRE`` 和 ``LOBATTO`` 都是合适的选择。"

msgid ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``\\ The maximum allowed angular order is set by the "
"row in the periodic table: "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,max_l=[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+]``. The default value is "
"[53,53,53,53]. Additionally, the minimum angular order can be set: "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,min_l=[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+]``. The default value is "
"[3,3,3,3]. This minimum is also modified to be at least :math:`2*l+1` where "
":math:`l` is the maximum angular momentum of the basis set."
msgstr ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``\\ 允许的最大角向阶数由元素周期表中的行设定：\\ "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,max_l=[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+]``\\ 。默认值为 "
"[53,53,53,53]。此外，还可以设置最小角向阶数：\\ "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,min_l=[Row1,Row2,Row3,Row4+]``\\ 。默认值为 "
"[3,3,3,3]。该最小值还会被修改为至少 :math:`2*l+1`\\ ，其中 :math:`l` 是基组的最大角动量。"

msgid ""
"*crowd* is a parameter to control the reduction of the degree of quadrature "
"close to the nucleus, where points would otherwise be unnecessarily close "
"together; larger values of crowd mean less reduction thus larger grids. A "
"very large value of this parameter, or, conventionally, setting it to zero, "
"will switch off this feature. The exact formula used for capping the "
":math:`L_\\mathrm{max}` value at a radial point :math:`r_i` for an atom with"
" a Bragg radius of :math:`R^\\mathrm{Bragg}` is "
":math:`L_\\mathrm{max}=min(L_\\mathrm{max},max(L_\\mathrm{min},min((crowd*r_i/R^\\mathrm{Bragg})*(L_\\mathrm{max}+1),10^6)-1))`."
" ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"
msgstr ""
"*crowd* 是用于控制靠近原子核处求积阶数削减程度的参数，否则该区域的点会不必要地靠得太近；crowd "
"值越大，削减越少，网格越大。将该参数取非常大的值，或按惯例将其设为零，将关闭此功能。对于 Bragg 半径为 "
":math:`R^\\mathrm{Bragg}` 的原子，在径向点 :math:`r_i` 处限制 :math:`L_\\mathrm{max}` "
"取值所用的精确公式为 "
":math:`L_\\mathrm{max}=min(L_\\mathrm{max},max(L_\\mathrm{min},min((crowd*r_i/R^\\mathrm{Bragg})*(L_\\mathrm{max}+1),10^6)-1))`\\"
" 。\\ ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"

msgid ""
"``ANGLEVEL`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` is an option that defines a fixed "
"Lebedev order for three different radial zones defined by the ranges [1...\\"
" *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/3], [*N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/3+1...\\ *N*\\ "
":math:`_{rad}`/2] and [*N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/2+1...\\ *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`] "
"with *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}` being the number of radial quadrature points and "
"the order is from close to nucleus to far distant radial points. The idea of"
" this definition is that only low Lebedev orders are needed in the first and"
" second zone while higher orders are required in the outer third zone in "
"order to achieve reasonable accuracies for the integration. It is possible "
"to choose between seven different schemes ``ANGLEVEL``\\ =1 to "
"``ANGLEVEL``\\ =7 where the grid sizes increases in that order. Fairly "
"accurate results should be accessible with intermediate levels "
"``ANGLEVEL``\\ =3,4. It is also possible to select ``ANGLEVEL``\\ =8 in "
"which case the :math:`L=59` (1202-point) Lebedev grid is used at each radial"
" point for highly accurate integrations."
msgstr ""
"``ANGLEVEL`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` 是一个为三个不同径向区间定义固定 Lebedev "
"阶数的选项，这些区间由范围 [1...\\ *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/3]、[*N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/3+1...\\"
" *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/2] 和 [*N*\\ :math:`_{rad}`/2+1...\\ *N*\\ "
":math:`_{rad}`] 定义，其中 *N*\\ :math:`_{rad}` "
"为径向求积点的数目，顺序为从靠近原子核到远离原子核的径向点。这样定义的思路是：第一和第二区间只需较低的 Lebedev "
"阶数，而外部的第三区间需要较高的阶数才能获得合理的积分精度。可以在 ``ANGLEVEL``\\=1 到 ``ANGLEVEL``\\=7 "
"这七种不同方案之间选择，网格大小按此顺序递增。采用中间档位 ``ANGLEVEL``\\=3,4 即可获得相当精确的结果。也可以选择 "
"``ANGLEVEL``\\=8，此时每个径向点都使用 :math:`L=59`\\ （1202 点）的 Lebedev 网格进行高精度积分。"

msgid ""
"``PRUNING_INTEGRAND``\\ =\\ *SAD*,\\ *PW91*,\\ *PW91MOL* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``"
msgstr ""
"``PRUNING_INTEGRAND``\\ =\\ *SAD*,\\ *PW91*,\\ *PW91MOL* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``"

msgid "``FROM_MIN_ORDER=0,1``"
msgstr "``FROM_MIN_ORDER=0,1``"

msgid "``FACNEIGH|FAC_NEIGHBOUR|FAC_NEIGHBOR=facn``"
msgstr "``FACNEIGH|FAC_NEIGHBOUR|FAC_NEIGHBOR=facn``"

msgid ""
"The grid generation for the angular grid depends on the integration of a "
"test density functional around a sphere around each atom at a given radial "
"point. The procedure is that first a target value for the highest possible "
"Lebedev order :math:`L` is computed and then that starting from the lowest "
"value of :math:`L` (up-pruning) the integral is computed again until the "
"deviation to the target value gets smaller than the threshold specified by "
"the value for ``GRIDTHR_ANG``\\ =acca, see also section `Angular integration"
" grid <the_density_functional_program.html#angular-integration-grid-"
"angular>`__. It is also possible to start from the largest possible value of"
" :math:`L` by setting ``FROM_MIN_ORDER``\\ =0 ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` "
"(down-pruning) and so the optimal value of :math:`L` will then be found by "
"seeking for the first one where the angular threshold is no longer obeyed. "
"This option is expected to be more accurate but can also lead to larger grid"
" sizes than the default option of ``FROM_MIN_ORDER``\\ =1."
msgstr ""
"角向网格的生成依赖于在给定径向点处围绕每个原子的球面上对一个测试密度泛函进行积分。具体过程是：先计算最高可能 Lebedev 阶数 :math:`L` "
"的目标值，然后从最低的 :math:`L` 值开始（向上修剪）重新计算积分，直到与目标值的偏差小于 ``GRIDTHR_ANG``\\=acca "
"所指定的阈值，另见 `角向积分网格 <the_density_functional_program.html#angular-integration-"
"grid-angular>`__ 一节。也可以通过设置 ``FROM_MIN_ORDER``\\=0 ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` "
"从最大的 :math:`L` 值开始（向下修剪），此时将通过寻找第一个不再满足角向阈值的值来确定 :math:`L` "
"的最优值。该选项预计更为精确，但与默认选项 ``FROM_MIN_ORDER``\\=1 相比也可能导致更大的网格。"

msgid ""
"One can choose between the three different integrands "
"``PRUNING_INTEGRAND``\\ =\\ *SAD*,\\ *PW91*,\\ *PW91MOL* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``. *SAD* just defines a superposition of Slater "
"atomic densities, *PW91* is a pseudo-density functional based on the PW91 xc"
" functional and *PW91MOL* is a refinement of *PW91* where the procedure to "
"find the optimal value of :math:`L` is slightly different (e.g., a linear "
"regression is performed in order to determine :math:`L` with this "
"integrand). Note that *PW91MOL* is set by default and is available both with"
" ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` and  ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``. In contrast, "
"integrands *SAD* and *PW91* can only be used with ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``."
msgstr ""
"可以在三种不同的被积函数 ``PRUNING_INTEGRAND``\\=\\ *SAD*,\\ *PW91*,\\ *PW91MOL* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 之间选择。\\ *SAD* 只是定义 Slater 原子密度的叠加，\\ *PW91* 是基于 "
"PW91 xc 泛函的一个赝密度泛函，而 *PW91MOL* 是 *PW91* 的改进版，其寻找 :math:`L` "
"最优值的过程略有不同（例如，使用这种被积函数时会通过线性回归来确定 :math:`L`\\ ）。注意，默认设置为 *PW91MOL*\\ ，且它在 "
"``dftgrid.png?nolink&50`` 和 ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 下都可用。相比之下，被积函数 *SAD* 和 "
"*PW91* 只能与 ``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 一起使用。"

msgid "``VORONOI,$m_\\mu$,vortyp``"
msgstr "``VORONOI,$m_\\mu$,vortyp``"

msgid ""
"``VORONOI_SCHEME``\\ =\\ *murray*,\\ *becke*,\\ *stratmann* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``"
msgstr ""
"``VORONOI_SCHEME``\\ =\\ *murray*,\\ *becke*,\\ *stratmann* "
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50``"

msgid "``SIZEADJ=becke,treutler,none``"
msgstr "``SIZEADJ=becke,treutler,none``"

msgid "``BECKE_MMU=mmu``"
msgstr "``BECKE_MMU=mmu``"

msgid "``MURRAY_MMU=mmu``"
msgstr "``MURRAY_MMU=mmu``"

msgid "``PRUNING_VORONOI_PAIRS=all,atom``"
msgstr "``PRUNING_VORONOI_PAIRS=all,atom``"

msgid ""
"Controls Becke-Voronoi partitioning of space. By default, the algorithm of "
"C. W. Murray, N. C. Handy and G. J. Laming, `Mol. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1080/00268979300100651>`__ **78**, 997 (1993) is "
"used, with :math:`m_\\mu` defined by equation (24). The default value is 10."
" ``vortyp`` defines the type of grid weights to be computed: 1: raw  "
"weights,  2: full voronoi,  4: pair voronoi. The default is ``vortyp=2.``"
msgstr ""
"控制空间的Becke-Voronoi划分。默认采用C. W. Murray、N. C. Handy和G. J. Laming的算法，\\ `Mol. "
"Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1080/00268979300100651>`__ **78**, 997 "
"(1993)，其中 :math:`m_\\mu` 由方程(24)定义。默认值为10。\\ ``vortyp`` "
"定义要计算的网格权重类型：1：原始权重，2：完整voronoi，4：对voronoi。默认值为 ``vortyp=2.``\\ 。"

msgid ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` It is possible to choose between the three "
"different step functions ``VORONOI_SCHEME``\\ =\\ *murray*,\\ *becke* and "
"*stratmann*. The Murray and Becke scheme employ a recursive formula that "
"increases the steepness of the function. The recursion limit is given by its"
" *mmu* value. In case of *becke* the default value of :math:`m_\\mu`\\ =3 is"
" being used. This can be modified from the default for each case using the "
"options ``BECKE_MMU`` or ``MURRAY_MMU``."
msgstr ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 可以在三种不同的阶梯函数 ``VORONOI_SCHEME``\\=\\ *murray*,\\ "
"*becke* 和 *stratmann* 之间选择。Murray 和 Becke 方案采用递归公式来增大函数的陡度。递归极限由其 *mmu* "
"值给出。对于 *becke*\\ ，使用默认值 :math:`m_\\mu`\\=3。可以使用选项 ``BECKE_MMU`` 或 "
"``MURRAY_MMU`` 针对每种情形修改该默认值。"

msgid ""
"For heteronuclear molecules Molpro uses Treutler and Ahlrichs atomic size "
"adjustment for the smoothing function `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.469408>`__ **102**, 346 (1995) (Eq.(13)). "
"Alternatively, the scheme by Becke `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.454033>`__ **88**, 2547 (1988). can be used by "
"setting ``SIZEADJ``\\ =\\ *becke*. Possible choices for ``SIZEADJ`` are "
"*becke*, *treutler* and *none*\\ ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``, the latter "
"meaning that no size adjustment is being used."
msgstr ""
"对于异核分子，Molpro 对平滑函数使用 Treutler 和 Ahlrichs 的原子尺寸调节 `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.469408>`__ **102**, 346 (1995)（式 (13)）。也可以通过设置 "
"``SIZEADJ``\\=\\ *becke* 使用 Becke 的方案 `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.454033>`__ **88**, 2547 (1988)。\\ ``SIZEADJ`` "
"的可能取值为 *becke*\\ 、\\ *treutler* 和 *none*\\ ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``\\ "
"，后者表示不使用尺寸调节。"

msgid ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` On-the-fly grid pruning can be expensive for large "
"molecules because of the cubic scaling of Voronoi partitioning. Pruning is "
"performed in under mpp parallelisation, with each process pruning each atom."
" If it is still too expensive, Voronoi partitioning can be limited for the "
"pruning algorithm to quadratic scaling: "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,pruning_voronoi_pairs=ATOM`` but can result in a less "
"accurate grid."
msgstr ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 对于大分子，由于 Voronoi 划分具有三次方标度，动态网格修剪的开销可能很大。修剪在 mpp "
"并行化下进行，每个进程负责修剪每个原子。如果开销仍然过大，可以在修剪算法中将 Voronoi 划分限制为二次方标度：\\ "
"``GRID,name=PRUNED,pruning_voronoi_pairs=ATOM``\\ ，但这可能导致网格精度下降。"

msgid "``WEIGHT_CUT|WCUT=thr``"
msgstr "``WEIGHT_CUT|WCUT=thr``"

msgid ""
"Grid points very close to the nucleus can have very small grid weights which"
" can drop below machine precision (~10d-16) when the radial grid is very "
"large. These can be discarded with the option ``WEIGHT_CUT``\\ =\\ *thr*, "
"i.e., grid points with weights smaller than *thr* will then not be used in "
"the numerical integration anymore. While this can make the integration a "
"little bit more efficient, a truncation of the grid with this option can "
"prevent to achieve high accuracies in the numerical integration below, e.g.,"
" micro-hartree accuracies for energies. Therefore by default ``WEIGHT_CUT`` "
"is set to a very small number that is well below machine precision "
"(``WEIGHT_CUT``\\ =1d-20) so that effectively all grid points close to the "
"nucleus are taken into account for the integration."
msgstr ""
"非常靠近原子核的网格点的网格权重可能非常小，当径向网格很大时可能降至机器精度以下（约 10d-16）。可以使用选项 "
"``WEIGHT_CUT``\\=\\ *thr* 丢弃这些点，即权重小于 *thr* "
"的网格点将不再用于数值积分。虽然这可以让积分稍微更高效一些，但用该选项截断网格可能妨碍在后续数值积分中达到高精度，例如能量的微哈特里精度。因此默认情况下"
" ``WEIGHT_CUT`` 被设为一个远低于机器精度的极小数值（\\ "
"``WEIGHT_CUT``\\=1d-20），从而实际上所有靠近原子核的网格点都被纳入积分。"

msgid "``GRIDPRINT,key=value,$\\dots$``"
msgstr "``GRIDPRINT,key=value,$\\dots$``"

msgid ""
"The orientation of the atomic grids can be controlled with the option "
"``ORIENT`` that can take the values 0, 1 and 2. ``ORIENT``\\ =0 means that "
"the grids are not oriented with respect to the atomic coordinates. This, "
"however, can lead to non-invariant KS energies with respect to rotations of "
"the molecule which is particularly significant for small grids. The setting "
"``ORIENT``\\ =1 uses the method of B. G. Johnson *et al.* `Chem. Phys. Lett."
" <https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2614(94)00199-5>`__ **220**, 377 (1994) which"
" constructs rotationally invariant DFT grids. The method of Johnson *et al.*"
" uses, however, the whole molecule to determine the orientation on each atom"
" which might not be ideal for very large molecules or molecular clusters in "
"various applications (determination of conformer energy differences, "
"potential energy surfaces, or geometry optimisations). This can be resolved "
"by the setting ``ORIENT``\\ =2 which emphasises the local environment in the"
" orientation of the atomic grids. This is the current default in Molpro "
"(version 2023.1 and higher)."
msgstr ""
"原子网格的取向可以通过选项 ``ORIENT`` 控制，其取值为 0、1 和 2。\\ ``ORIENT``\\=0 "
"表示网格不随原子坐标取向。但这会导致 KS 能量对分子转动不具有不变性，这对小网格尤为明显。设置 ``ORIENT``\\=1 采用 B. G. "
"Johnson *等* 的方法 `Chem. Phys. Lett. "
"<https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2614(94)00199-5>`__ **220**, 377 "
"(1994)，它构造转动不变的 DFT 网格。然而，Johnson *等* "
"的方法使用整个分子来确定每个原子上的取向，对于各种应用（构象能差的确定、势能面或几何优化）中的超大分子或分子簇可能并不理想。设置 "
"``ORIENT``\\=2 可以解决这一问题，它在原子网格取向中更强调局部环境。这是 Molpro 当前版本（2023.1 及更高版本）的默认设置。"

msgid "= Adaptive Molpro Grid (AMG)"
msgstr "= 自适应 Molpro 网格（AMG）"

msgid ""
"By default Molpro generates a quadrature grid which prunes the angular grid "
"using an adaptive scheme which takes the molecular environment into account."
" Several pruning methods and functions can be set. The pruning method used "
"can be controlled via the option"
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，Molpro 生成的求积网格会采用考虑分子环境的自适应方案对角向网格进行修剪。可以设置多种修剪方法和函数。所使用的修剪方法可通过选项"

msgid "``GRID,prunmeth=[1-5]`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"
msgstr "``GRID,prunmeth=[1-5]`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"

msgid ""
"The pruning function :math:`\\mathcal{S}` (a spherical integral at the given"
" radial grid point) is computed for a model density using a superposition of"
" Slater's densities for the current geometry for the maximum angular grid "
"order set (:math:`L_\\mathrm{max}=59`) and then the respective algorithms "
"find the lowest possible value of :math:`L` (at each radial grid point) for "
"which the difference :math:`\\Delta "
"\\mathcal{S}(L)=|\\mathcal{S}(L_\\mathrm{max})-\\mathcal{S}(L)|` is below a "
"threshold given by the input parameter ``GRIDTHR``. The function "
":math:`\\mathcal{S}` can be adjusted with"
msgstr ""
"修剪函数 :math:`\\mathcal{S}`\\ （在给定径向网格点处的球面积分）针对模型密度计算，模型密度取当前几何结构下 Slater "
"密度的叠加，角向网格阶数取所设置的最大值（\\ :math:`L_\\mathrm{max}=59`\\ "
"）；然后，相应算法（在每个径向网格点处）找出使差值 :math:`\\Delta "
"\\mathcal{S}(L)=|\\mathcal{S}(L_\\mathrm{max})-\\mathcal{S}(L)|` 低于输入参数 "
"``GRIDTHR`` 所给阈值的最低可行 :math:`L` 值。函数 :math:`\\mathcal{S}` 可通过下式调整"

msgid "``GRID,prunefunc=[0-1]`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"
msgstr "``GRID,prunefunc=[0-1]`` ``dftgrid.png?nolink&50``"

msgid ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` There are three alternative types of pruned grids "
"that can be used; ``PRUNED``, ``NEESE`` and ``SG``. They can be selected by "
"setting the ``name`` option:"
msgstr ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 有三种可供使用的替代修剪网格类型：\\ ``PRUNED``\\ 、\\ ``NEESE`` 和 "
"``SG``\\ 。可以通过设置 ``name`` 选项来选择："

msgid "``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` The NEESE grid is a fixed-pruned grid."
msgstr "``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` NEESE 网格是固定修剪网格。"

msgid ""
"References: :math:`[1]` Krack, M., Köster, A.M., 1998. An adaptive numerical"
" integrator for molecular integrals. `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.475719>`__ **108**, 3226-3234. "
"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.475719"
msgstr ""
"References: :math:`[1]` Krack, M., Köster, A.M., 1998. An adaptive numerical"
" integrator for molecular integrals. `J. Chem. Phys. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.475719>`__ **108**, 3226-3234. "
"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.475719"

msgid ""
"``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` The fixed-pruned Standard Grid (SG) can be used:"
msgstr "``xcgrid.png?nolink&50`` 可以使用固定修剪的标准网格（SG）："

msgid ""
"``GRID,name=SG0\\\\`` ``GRID,name=SG1\\\\`` ``GRID,name=SG2\\\\`` or "
"``GRID,name=SG3\\\\``"
msgstr ""
"``GRID,name=SG0\\\\`` ``GRID,name=SG1\\\\`` ``GRID,name=SG2\\\\`` 或 "
"``GRID,name=SG3\\\\``"

msgid ""
"References: :math:`[1]` Chien, S.-H., Gill, P.M.W., 2006. SG-0: A small "
"standard grid for DFT quadrature on large systems. `J. Comput. Chem. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1002/jcc.20383>`__ **27**, 730-739. "
"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.20383 :math:`[2]` Gill, P.M.W., Johnson, B.G., "
"Pople, J.A., 1993. A standard grid for density functional calculations. "
"Chem. Phys. Let. 209, 506-512. https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2614(93)80125-9 "
":math:`[3]` Dasgupta, S. Herbert, J. M., 2017. Standard Grids for High-"
"Precision Integration of Modern Density Functionals: SG-2 and SG-3. `J. "
"Comput. Chem. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1002/jcc.24761>`__ **38**, 869–882. "
"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.24761"
msgstr ""
"References: :math:`[1]` Chien, S.-H., Gill, P.M.W., 2006. SG-0: A small "
"standard grid for DFT quadrature on large systems. `J. Comput. Chem. "
"<https://dx.doi.org/10.1002/jcc.20383>`__ **27**, 730-739. "
"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.20383 :math:`[2]` Gill, P.M.W., Johnson, B.G., "
"Pople, J.A., 1993. A standard grid for density functional calculations. "
"Chem. Phys. Let. 209, 506-512. https://doi.org/10.1016/0009-2614(93)80125-9 "
":math:`[3]` Dasgupta, S. Herbert, J. M., 2017. Standard Grids for High-"
"Precision Integration of Modern Density Functionals: SG-2 and SG-3. `J. "
"Comput. Chem. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1002/jcc.24761>`__ **38**, 869–882. "
"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.24761"

